# Security headers for every response served by the astra-3d-benchmark Worker (Workers Static Assets _headers).
# CSP is strict (same-origin everything, no 'unsafe-inline') with ONE compromise, 'unsafe-eval' in script-src:
#   script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' 'unsafe-eval'
#       the app bundle is same-origin. The KTX2 (Basis) transcoder compiles WebAssembly, and its Emscripten/embind
#       glue builds binding functions with `new Function(...)` inside the blob: worker, which inherits this page's
#       policy, so without 'unsafe-eval' the 3D model never finishes loading (verified in Chrome). To drop it,
#       the transcoder worker would have to be a same-origin file with its own CSP header instead of three's blob worker.
#   static.cloudflareinsights.com (script-src) and cloudflareinsights.com (connect-src): Cloudflare Web Analytics, auto-injected by the zone.
#   worker-src 'self' blob:               three.js KTX2Loader runs transcoder Web Workers from a blob: URL
#   img-src / connect-src blob: data:     GLTFLoader reads embedded textures through blob: URLs (ImageBitmap / fetch)
#   style-src 'self'                      Vite emits one CSS file; React sets styles through the CSSOM, which CSP allows
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' 'unsafe-eval' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' blob: data: https://cloudflareinsights.com; media-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), hid=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), publickey-credentials-get=(), serial=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
